  },
  {
    "q": "Is there a standard for transcreation?",
    "a": "None of the standards read for this page names transcreation in its scope. ISO 17100:2015 covers translation services, ISO 18587:2017 covers human post-editing of machine translation, and ISO 5060:2024 covers evaluating translation output. The Institute of Translation and Interpreting's Transcreation Code of Practice, August 2026, addresses it directly, as association guidelines."
  },
  {
    "q": "How is transcreation priced?",
    "a": "By the project, the hour or the day, according to the Institute of Translation and Interpreting's code, which says transcreation is never paid per word and is usually priced above traditional translation. Published translation rate cards collected in September 2026 put professional English to Simplified Chinese at roughly $0.08 to $0.18 per source word, with no method behind the band."
  },
  {
    "q": "Can AI do transcreation?",
    "a": "The published views point different ways. The Institute of Translation and Interpreting's code takes the position that generative AI is not useful for transcreation work. A global advertiser trade body survey from March 2025 found 34 percent of respondents at 50 brands using it in translation, with 23 percent more planning to. Settle AI use and data handling in the brief."
  }
];
